    "id": "gpu-memory-path",
    "caption": "Every decode step streams the weights from VRAM through L2 into the SMs, so memory bandwidth, not Tensor Core speed, usually sets the pace.",
    "alt": "The CPU tokenizes requests and launches work on the GPU over PCIe. Inside the GPU, model weights and the KV cache live in VRAM (HBM). For each step they are read through the shared L2 cache into the streaming multiprocessors, where Tensor Cores perform the matrix maths and registers and shared memory hold working data. The VRAM-to-SM path is labelled as the bandwidth bottleneck for decode.",
